What is Rate Limiting?

Rate limiting is a mechanism that limits the number of requests a user/client can make within a specific time period.

Example
Suppose an API allows:
100 requests per minute
If a user sends:
Request 1 ✔
Request 2 ✔
...
Request 100 ✔
Request 101 ❌ Too Many Requests (HTTP 429)
The 101st request is rejected until the time window resets.
